open-vm-tools: native Wayland drag and drop and copy/paste for vmware-user

On a Wayland session, vmware-user's dndcp plugin drags and copies through
Xwayland, which depends on the compositor carrying drags and the clipboard
between X11 and Wayland clients. KWin doesn't do that for vmware-user: drags
from the host never drop, and copying from the guest does nothing.

This adds native Wayland backends, each chosen at startup when the session
is Wayland and the compositor has the protocols, with the existing X11 code
as the fallback (e.g. on GNOME):

- DnDUIWayland: drag and drop through a full-output wlr-layer-shell surface,
  whose input region is the drag detection window, a uinput pointer starting
  wl_data_device drags from its press, and a held uinput button keeping a
  guest drag alive while the host asks about it. Needs zwlr_layer_shell_v1,
  wl_data_device_manager v3 and wp_viewporter.

- CopyPasteUIWayland: copy/paste of text, RTF, PNG and files through
  ext-data-control-v1 or wlr-data-control-unstable-v1, with vmblock-backed
  file transfer on first access.

VMTOOLS_DND_BACKEND and VMTOOLS_CP_BACKEND (x11 or wayland) force a choice.
Build with --with-wayland (default auto; needs wayland-client and
wayland-scanner). The Wayland protocol XML is included under
services/plugins/dndcp/wayland.

Made against the stable-13.1.0 tag, relative to its open-vm-tools/
directory; apply with patch -p1 there. This patch is under the licences of
the files it changes: LGPL-2.1 for the dndcp plugin, GPL-2.0 for its
Makefile.am and open-vm-tools' licence for configure.ac; the protocol XML
keeps its own MIT-style licences.

Development history: the wayland-dnd branch of
https://github.com/northbymidwest/open-vm-tools

